I
摘要
中国城市化进程中,人口增长和经济活动提升对交通系统提出了更高要求。
传统交通模式带来的噪声、空气污染和化石燃料依赖等问题日益严重。地铁作为
城市交通的重要组成部分,以其高效、环保和低土地占用优势,逐渐成为解决城
市交通问题的关键。但在建设过程中,地质环境的复杂性,尤其是湖泊、河流等
富水地质条件,给隧道施工带来安全隐患。因此,对这些风险路段进行安全性能
评估和采取相应措施,对于确保地铁建设顺利进行至关重要。本文以重庆市 15
号线工程实例为研究背景,对下穿双龙湖段进行了隧道掘进机(Tunnel Boring
Machine, TBM)风险控制。采用 FLAC3D 软件对下穿双龙湖地段进行开挖模拟,
结合优化的层次分析法和因子分析法,确立了 11 种影响因素各自的权重系数,
为双龙湖风险分析提供了科学依据。具体研究工作包括:
(1)结合绣湖路站-T3 航站楼站的不同地质条件和施工环境下的适应性进
行了全面分析,进行了 TBM 和盾构机适用条件的对比分析和选型研究,根据沿
线岩土体特点、地质条件及土层参数等,对 TBM 盾构推力参数、刀盘刀具类型、
刀盘扭矩及掘进参数等各参数进行了在施工过程中的适应性分析,满足施工环境
对于施工机械要求的参数的选取;
(2) 针对下穿双龙湖段的环境与地质特点,采用 TBM 对下穿双龙湖段进
行施工掘进的数值模拟,并结合实际监测数据进行对比分析,验证了带压推进施
工的可行性;
(3)针对双龙湖段特殊的地质条件和施工风险,通过数值模拟方法探讨了
在不同施工条件下 TBM 施工过程。采用 FLAC3D 软件,模拟了不同注浆厚度、
注浆强度和是否做围堰的方案,并根据数值模拟结果对带压推进施工方案的可行
性及其优缺点进行了分析比较,为选择合适的施工方案提供依据;
(4)采用层次分析法对 TBM 施工进行权重分析,识别量化施工过程中的
主要风险因素。通过构建风险评估模型,对风险原因进行分类,通过 MATLAB
获取相应权重,揭示各风险因素对施工安全和施工效率的相对重要性,并提出相
应预防措施。
关键词:TBM 施工,适宜性研究,数值模拟,施工风险控制,层次分析法


II
ABSTRACT
The urbanization process in China has put forward higher demands on the transportation system due to population growth and the enhancement of economic activities. Traditional transportation modes have brought about increasingly severe problems such as noise, air pollution, and dependence on fossil fuels. As an important part of urban transportation, subways, with their advantages of high efficiency, environmental friendliness, and low land occupation, are gradually becoming key to solving urban transportation problems. However, the complexity of geological environments, especially water-rich geological conditions such as lakes and rivers, poses safety hazards to tunnel construction. Therefore, conducting safety performance assessments and taking corresponding measures for these risk sections is crucial to ensure the smooth progress of subway construction. This paper takes the example of the Chongqing Metro Line 15 project, and carries out risk control for the tunnel boring machine (TBM) when passing through the Shuanglong Lake section. The FLAC3D software is used to simulate the excavation of the Shuanglong Lake section, and the optimized Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP) and factor analysis method are combined to establish the weight coefficients of 11 influencing factors, providing a scientific basis for risk analysis of Shuanglong Lake. The specific research work includes: (1) A comprehensive analysis was conducted on the adaptability under different geological conditions and construction environments between Xiuhu Road Station and T3 Terminal Station. A comparative analysis and selection research of the applicability of TBM and shield machines were carried out. According to the characteristics of the rock-soil mass along the line, geological conditions, and soil layer parameters, the adaptability analysis of TBM shield thrust parameters, cutter disc tool types, cutter disc torque, and excavation parameters was conducted during the construction process, to meet the requirements of the construction environment for the selection of construction machinery parameters; (2) In view of the environmental and geological characteristics of the section passing through Shuanglong Lake, TBM was used for numerical simulation of construction excavation of the section, and the feasibility of pressurized advancement construction was verified by comparing it with actual monitoring data; (3) In response to the special geological conditions and construction risks of the Shuanglong Lake section, the TBM construction process under different construction conditions was discussed through numerical simulation methods. The FLAC3D software was used to simulate different grouting thicknesses, grouting strengths, and whether to build a cofferdam, and the feasibility and advantages and disadvantages of the pressurized advancement construction plan were analyzed and compared based on the results of numerical simulation, providing a basis for selecting the appropriate construction plan; (4) The Analytic Hierarchy Process was used for weight analysis of TBM construction to identify and quantify the main risk factors in the construction process.


III
By constructing a risk assessment model, the causes of risk were classified, and the corresponding weights were obtained through MATLAB, revealing the relative importance of various risk factors to construction safety and efficiency, and corresponding preventive measures were proposed.
KEY WORDS:TBM construction, suitability study, numerical simulation,
construction risk control, Analytic Hierarchy Process


